```java
private CustomsHoldResponse doHold(CustomsHoldRequest request) {
    BagRow snapshot = findBag(request.bagTag());
    if (snapshot == null) throw notFound;
    // 与 load 保持一致的加锁顺序：先航段后行李，避免死锁
    String loadedLegId = snapshot.loadedLegId();
    if (loadedLegId != null) lockLeg(loadedLegId);
    BagRow bag = lockBag(request.bagTag());
    // 状态校验
    if (CUSTOMS_HOLD) -> conflict with location
    if (DELIVERED) -> conflict 已到达最终目的地
    if (SHORT_UNLOADED) -> conflict 已丢失/短卸
    // loaded leg may have changed between snapshot and lock
    String currentLoaded = bag.loadedLegId();
    LegRow loadedLeg = null;
    if (currentLoaded != null) {
        if (!currentLoaded.equals(loadedLegId)) {
            loadedLeg = lockLeg(currentLoaded); // 快照后变更，补锁新航段
        } else {
            loadedLeg = findLeg(currentLoaded); // already locked; re-read locked row
        }
        if (LEG_SEALED.equals(loadedLeg.status())) throw conflict("行李已处于 SEALED 航段...");
        // ARRIVED with loaded_leg_id set shouldn't happen; treat as conflict too? If ARRIVED, load_record deleted — removal would fail → rollback per spec. Actually if leg ARRIVED and bag still shows loaded_leg_id, that's transient inconsistency that can't happen since arrive clears both in one tx. I'll handle: if not OPEN → conflict.
    }
    // holdKey uniqueness
    if (findHold(request.holdKey()) != null) throw conflict("holdKey 已存在");
    // remove from OPEN manifest
    if (loadedLeg != null) {
        int removed = jdbcTemplate.update("DELETE FROM load_record WHERE bag_tag = ? AND leg_id = ?", bagTag, legId);
        if (removed != 1) throw new IllegalStateException("从航段清单移除失败，整次回滚");
        jdbcTemplate.update("UPDATE leg SET version = ? WHERE leg_id = ?", loadedLeg.version()+1, legId);
    }
    Instant now = clock.get();
    jdbcTemplate.update("UPDATE bag SET status=?, loaded_leg_id=NULL WHERE bag_tag=?", CUSTOMS_HOLD, bagTag);
    jdbcTemplate.update("INSERT INTO customs_hold (...) VALUES (...)", ...);
    insertEvent(bagTag, EVT_CUSTOMS_HOLD, currentLoaded, request.location());
    return new CustomsHoldResponse(...);
}
```

Wait — leg version bump on removal: should I bump? The manifest changed. Load bumps version. For consistency and to make concurrent seal with stale expectedVersion fail, bump. But hmm — if hold removes bag and bumps version, then a seal submitted with the old expectedVersion gets 409. That's the correct optimistic-concurrency behavior. Yes bump.

Also note: findLeg after lockLeg for the same row — lockLeg already returns the row; if loadedLegId unchanged, I already have the locked row from the first lockLeg call. Restructure:

```java
LegRow loadedLeg = null;
if (loadedLegId != null) loadedLeg = lockLeg(loadedLegId);
BagRow bag = lockBag(...);
String currentLoaded = bag.loadedLegId();
if (currentLoaded != null && !currentLoaded.equals(loadedLegId)) {
    loadedLeg = lockLeg(currentLoaded); // 极端情况：快照后装载航段变更，补锁
}
```
If currentLoaded == null but loadedLegId != null (arrive committed in between): then no removal needed, loadedLeg stale — set loadedLeg = null. Handle: 
```java
if (currentLoaded == null) loadedLeg = null;
else if (!currentLoaded.equals(loadedLegId)) loadedLeg = lockLeg(currentLoaded);
```

Then check loadedLeg status: if not OPEN → 409 (SEALED → "已 SEALED 不得暂扣"; ARRIVED → shouldn't happen but 409 anyway).

Wait, but there's a subtlety: if loadedLegId != null initially, we locked that leg. If bag's current loaded is null now, we hold a lock on a leg unnecessarily — harmless.

